## Scope and limitations

This library reads and writes local CFB / MSG / EML files only — it does not implement IMAP,
SMTP, or POP3 and does not connect to mail servers. TNEF (`winmail.dat`) is not parsed or
generated. There is no dedicated calendar or appointment API, though calendar-specific MAPI
properties can be accessed generically via `SetProperty()` / `GetPropertyValue()`. The library
requires .NET 8.0 or later; classic .NET Framework (4.x) is not supported.

For IMAP/SMTP/POP3 connectivity, calendar support, and broader format coverage, see
[Aspose.Email for .NET — Enterprise Edition](https://products.aspose.com/email/net/).

## Development and testing

Build the library and run the xUnit test suite from the repository root:

```bash
dotnet build src/Aspose.Email.Foss/Aspose.Email.Foss.csproj -c Release
dotnet test tests/Aspose.Email.Foss.Tests/Aspose.Email.Foss.Tests.csproj -c Release
```

